## 6. Data model changes

### 6.1 New `Reminder` fields (all optional so old rows stay valid)
```ts
export type ReminderRepeatFreq = "daily" | "weekly" | "monthly" | "yearly";

export interface ReminderRecurrence {
  freq: ReminderRepeatFreq;
  interval: number;            // >= 1
  byWeekday?: number[];        // 0 = Sunday .. 6 = Saturday; weekly only
  byMonthDay?: number;         // 1..31; monthly only (default: day of startAt)
  until?: number;              // epoch ms, inclusive end of the series
  count?: number;              // total occurrences, including the first
  exdates?: number[];          // occurrence start times (epoch ms) that are skipped
}

export interface Reminder {
  /* existing fields unchanged */
  startAt?: number;            // event start; for events triggerAt = startAt - leadMinutes*60000
  endAt?: number;
  allDay?: boolean;
  leadMinutes?: number;        // default 0
  location?: string;
  notes?: string;
  recurrence?: ReminderRecurrence | null;
  occurrencesFired?: number;   // counts toward `count`
  snoozedUntil?: number | null;
  firedAt?: number | null;     // last time an alert was shown
  missedCount?: number;        // occurrences skipped while the app was closed
  source?: "manual" | "ics";
  externalUid?: string;        // iCalendar UID
  externalInstance?: string | null; // RECURRENCE-ID for a moved single occurrence
  externalSequence?: number;   // iCalendar SEQUENCE, for update detection
  externalModified?: number;   // LAST-MODIFIED as epoch ms
  rruleRaw?: string | null;    // original RRULE text, kept for transparency
}
```

Semantics to implement exactly:
- `triggerAt` remains **the time the alert fires** (this keeps every existing query working). For an event, `triggerAt = startAt - leadMinutes * 60_000`. For a plain reminder, `startAt` is undefined and `triggerAt` is as before.
- A reminder with `recurrence` is **one row per series**. After an occurrence fires, the row stays `pending`, `startAt`/`triggerAt` advance to the next occurrence, `occurrencesFired` increments, `firedAt` is set. When the series is exhausted (past `until`, or `occurrencesFired >= count`, or the next occurrence does not exist), set `status: "fired"` and `recurrence` stays as history.
- `snoozedUntil`: while set and in the future, `triggerAt` is treated as that time. Implement by **writing the snooze time into `triggerAt`** and remembering the real occurrence in `startAt` (so a snoozed repeating event still advances correctly afterwards). Clear `snoozedUntil` when it fires.

