## 7. iCalendar (.ics) parser: `src/data/ics.ts`

Pure functions, no DOM, no Dexie, fully unit-tested. Public API:

```ts
export interface ParsedEvent {
  uid: string;
  instanceId: string | null;      // RECURRENCE-ID as a stable string, else null
  title: string;                  // SUMMARY, trimmed; "(No title)" if empty
  startAt: number;                // epoch ms (for all-day: start of day in device zone)
  endAt: number | null;
  allDay: boolean;
  location: string;
  notes: string;                  // DESCRIPTION, control characters stripped, max 2000 chars
  recurrence: ReminderRecurrence | null;
  rruleRaw: string | null;
  leadMinutes: number | null;     // from the first usable VALARM TRIGGER, else null
  sequence: number;               // SEQUENCE, default 0
  modifiedAt: number | null;      // LAST-MODIFIED or DTSTAMP as epoch ms
  warnings: ParseWarning[];
}
export type ParseWarning = "rrule-simplified" | "timezone-assumed" | "no-title";

export interface ParseResult {
  events: ParsedEvent[];
  skipped: { title: string | null; reason: string }[];  // cancelled, no start, unreadable
}
export function parseIcs(text: string, opts?: { deviceTimeZone?: string }): ParseResult;
```

### 7.1 Parsing rules
1. **Normalise input:** strip a UTF-8 BOM; split on `\r\n`, `\n` or `\r`.
2. **Unfold lines:** a line starting with a space or tab continues the previous line (remove the break plus that one leading whitespace character).
3. **Property syntax:** `NAME;PARAM=value;PARAM2="quoted;value":VALUE`. Split on the first unquoted `:`; parameters on unquoted `;`. Names are case-insensitive.
4. **Text unescaping** for SUMMARY, DESCRIPTION, LOCATION: `\\n`/`\\N` to newline, `\\,` to comma, `\\;` to semicolon, `\\\\` to backslash.
5. **Only read `BEGIN:VEVENT ... END:VEVENT` blocks.** Ignore `VTIMEZONE` content entirely (rely on IANA names in `TZID`). `VALARM` blocks nested inside a `VEVENT` are read for `TRIGGER` only.
6. **Skip with a reason** (put in `skipped`, never throw): `STATUS:CANCELLED`; missing `DTSTART`; unparseable date; missing `UID` (generate a deterministic id from title+start instead, and mark no warning).
7. **Dates** (`DTSTART`, `DTEND`, `RECURRENCE-ID`, `EXDATE`, `UNTIL`):
   - `...Z` suffix = UTC.
   - `;VALUE=DATE:YYYYMMDD` = all-day; `startAt` is local midnight in the device zone; `endAt` in iCalendar is **exclusive** (the day after), so subtract one day for display only (store as given minus nothing; document in a comment).
   - `;TZID=Zone/Name:YYYYMMDDTHHMMSS` = wall-clock time in that IANA zone. Convert with `Intl.DateTimeFormat` (no library): compute the UTC instant whose wall-clock time in `Zone` equals the given fields, using a two-pass offset correction so it is right across DST changes.
   - No `Z`, no `TZID` (floating) = device zone.
   - **Unknown or Windows-style TZID** (e.g. `Eastern Standard Time`) that `Intl` rejects: fall back to the device zone and add warning `timezone-assumed`.
8. **DTEND vs DURATION:** use `DTEND` if present; else `DTSTART + DURATION` (ISO-8601, e.g. `PT1H30M`); else `endAt = null`.
9. **VALARM `TRIGGER`:** only relative negative durations before start (`-PT15M`, `-P1D`) map to `leadMinutes` (round to whole minutes; cap at 7 days). Absolute triggers and triggers relative to END are ignored. Use the **smallest positive lead** among alarms if several exist (the soonest-firing one is the most useful single alert).
10. **RECURRENCE-ID:** an event with `RECURRENCE-ID` is a moved/edited single occurrence of a series. It becomes its own `ParsedEvent` with `instanceId` set. The importer (section 8) adds that original occurrence time to the master series' `exdates` so it is not duplicated.
11. **Size/safety limits** (enforce in the importer, but the parser must also be defensive): process at most 5000 events per file; truncate notes to 2000 chars; truncate title to 300; strip ASCII control characters except newline.

### 7.2 RRULE mapping
Parse `RRULE:FREQ=...;INTERVAL=...;BYDAY=...;BYMONTHDAY=...;COUNT=...;UNTIL=...`, plus `EXDATE` lines (comma-separated lists allowed, multiple lines allowed).

Supported -> `ReminderRecurrence`:
| RRULE | Maps to |
|---|---|
| `FREQ=DAILY[;INTERVAL=n]` | `daily`, `interval n` |
| `FREQ=WEEKLY[;INTERVAL=n][;BYDAY=MO,WE]` | `weekly`, `byWeekday [1,3]` (no BYDAY: weekday of start) |
| `FREQ=MONTHLY[;INTERVAL=n][;BYMONTHDAY=d]` | `monthly`, `byMonthDay d` (none: day of start) |
| `FREQ=YEARLY[;INTERVAL=n]` | `yearly` |
| `COUNT=n` | `count n` |
| `UNTIL=...` | `until` (inclusive; if date-only, end of that local day) |
| `EXDATE` | `exdates` (epoch ms of each skipped occurrence) |

**Not supported (degrade, do not fail):** `BYSETPOS`, ordinal weekdays like `BYDAY=1MO`/`-1FR` ("first Monday", "last Friday"), `BYYEARDAY`, `BYWEEKNO`, `BYHOUR/BYMINUTE/BYSECOND`, `FREQ=HOURLY/MINUTELY/SECONDLY`, `RDATE`. For these: set `recurrence = null`, keep `rruleRaw`, import the **next future occurrence only** (compute the next occurrence from the start using a minimal expansion if you can, otherwise just `startAt`) and add warning `rrule-simplified`.

